  m_Name: Siproeta epaphus
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ButterflyData
  speciesName: Mariposa Siproeta epaphus epaphus
  description: "La Siproeta epaphus epaphus, tambi\xE9n conocida como la mariposa
    de las patas largas, es una mariposa perteneciente a la familia Nymphalidae y
    al g\xE9nero Siproeta.\r\n\r\nCaracter\xEDsticas principales:\r\n\r\nEs una mariposa
    de tama\xF1o medio, con una envergadura de aproximadamente 5 a 7 cm.\r\nSu coloraci\xF3n
    var\xEDa, pero generalmente presenta alas de color marr\xF3n con manchas y patrones
    en tonos naranjas, amarillos y blancos en el reverso de las alas.\r\nEn el dorso
    de sus alas, tiene un dise\xF1o bastante distintivo con l\xEDneas y puntos que
    le ayudan a camuflarse entre la vegetaci\xF3n."
  speciesNameEn: Butterfly Siproeta epaphus epaphus
  descriptionEn: 'The Siproeta epaphus epaphus , also known as the long-legged butterfly
    , is a butterfly belonging to the Nymphalidae family and the genus Siproeta .

    

    Main
    features:

    

    It is a medium-sized butterfly, with a wingspan of approximately
    5 to 7 cm .

    Its coloration varies, but it generally has brown wings with
    spots and patterns in shades of orange, yellow and white on the underside of
    the wings.

    On the back of its wings, it has a rather distinctive design
    with lines and dots that help it camouflage itself among the vegetation.'
